# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# Shell scripts MUST be LF — defense-in-depth against autocrlf=true (g-115-869).
# Without these explicit rules, `* text=auto` is heuristic-only and git's
# enforcement is not guaranteed; charlie's 2026-05-16 rc=127 incident (CRLF
# bash refusing to exec) reproduced because `_runtime.sh` was attr=text=auto,
# not attr=text eol=lf. Sibling fix: g-115-868 routes insight-trigger-sweep
# through _rt.py to bypass bash entirely.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf

# Git hooks are shell scripts too, but EXTENSIONLESS — the *.sh/*.bash rules
# above don't match their names, so pin them to LF explicitly. autocrlf=true
# would otherwise check them out as CRLF on a fresh clone and break execution
# (same g-115-869 rc=127 class). Covers pre-commit/post-commit/pre-push and any
# future hook — critical because a fresh-clone machine (machine-2, CI) is exactly
# where the pre-push M2 tag gate must still run.
core/githooks/* text eol=lf

# Cross-machine merge self-resolution for APPEND-ONLY agent ledgers (2026-07-03,
# user-directed GitHub-sync bolstering). When the same agent identity commits
# from two machines (e.g. container alpha + desktop alpha), both sides append
# at EOF from a common base — a guaranteed textual conflict that would wedge
# iteration-push.sh's integrate step every iteration. merge=union keeps BOTH
# sides' lines (no data loss; consumers scan whole files, order-insensitive).
# SCOPE IS EVIDENCE-GATED: only files with ZERO historical deleted lines
# qualify (probe: git log -p, count '^-{' lines == 0). journal.jsonl (index
# rewrites), changelog.jsonl (pruning), experience.jsonl (archival), and
# aspirations.jsonl (RMW status updates) are NOT union-safe — a union there
# would resurrect pruned/edited lines. Those RMW ledgers instead route to the
# record-aware merge=ayoai-ledger driver below (g-115-2767).
# CORRECTED IN PLACE (g-115-4357): this paragraph used to say the driver "unions
# them by record/counter rather than by line — so they self-heal like the union
# files without resurrecting pruned/edited history". That premise was measured
# FALSE. Record-keying changes what counts as a DUPLICATE, never whether a
# ONE-SIDED record SURVIVES, so an id-union resurrects exactly as thoroughly as a
# line-union: reproduced on all three routed basenames (an archive sweep removal
# and a journal rotation both came back; an experience-archive set_field edit was
# silently REVERTED to its pre-edit form). What actually applies a removal is the
# driver reading %O and dropping a record the BASE holds that one side no longer
# does — which is why this routing is safe now and was not before.
agents/*/skill-invocations.jsonl merge=union
agents/*/health/*.jsonl merge=union

# Record-level cross-machine merge for the RMW agent ledgers that merge=union
# CANNOT safely handle (id-keyed records, counter rollups, pruned/archived
# history). The ayoai-ledger driver (core/scripts/git-merge-ayoai-ledger.sh)
# resolves cross-box conflicts by RECORD-LEVEL commutative union, reusing
# coordination_merge.py's own-cloud handlers — so iteration-push.sh's integrate
# step self-heals instead of aborting (g-115-2767, from zeta's g-115-2727
# investigation: experience/changelog/meta conflicts stranded MIND commits
# g-335-157..159). Driver registered per-clone by install-git-hooks.sh (git
# driver config is NOT version-controlled, same mechanism as core.hooksPath).
# NOT union — a union resurrects pruned/archived/edited records (the exact reason
# these are excluded from the union block above), and that is true of a
# RECORD-keyed union as much as a line-keyed one. The driver is base-aware for
# precisely this reason: %O is what separates "the peer never had this record"
# from "the peer DELETED it" (g-115-4357).
# SCOPE CORRECTED IN PLACE (g-115-9132): "the driver is base-aware" was true of
# the driver but NOT of all six paths it routes. %O reaches merge_bytes and is
# used by the _JSONL_ID_UNION branch, which covers experience / experience-archive
# / journal (plus the counter file). changelog.jsonl and aspirations.jsonl have no entry in that
# set: they resolve through coordination_merge.merge_handler_for, whose handler
# signature is (local, remote) -> bytes and which therefore never sees the base at
# all. Measured 2026-09-06 (alpha worker Body, cc-10) by driving merge_bytes with
# a real base: a record the base held and one side retired came back on BOTH of
# those paths, while the experience path correctly dropped it — the same
# positive-controlled probe in one run. The driver now composes a base-aware
# delete filter over the registry handler for exactly those two agent paths, so
# the handler keeps its field-level merge and the removal still propagates. The
# world queue is deliberately NOT in scope: its removal is represented out of band
# (archive record + the daemon archive_sweep reconciler), which
# coordination_merge.merge_aspirations documents at length.
agents/*/experience.jsonl merge=ayoai-ledger
agents/*/experience-archive.jsonl merge=ayoai-ledger
agents/*/experience-meta.json merge=ayoai-ledger
agents/*/changelog.jsonl merge=ayoai-ledger
agents/*/journal.jsonl merge=ayoai-ledger
agents/*/aspirations.jsonl merge=ayoai-ledger

# Section-level cross-machine merge for the NARRATIVE daily journal. The rule
# above covers journal.jsonl (the INDEX); nothing covered the daily .md the
# index points AT, so it had no merge routing at all. journal-append.sh creates
# it on the day's first write, so one agent identity running on two boxes has
# BOTH boxes create the same path with no common ancestor — a textbook add/add
# that recurs EVERY calendar day for EVERY multi-box agent and aborts the whole
# merge, stranding unrelated ledger work with it (g-115-3425, root-caused in
# g-115-3422: the authoritative conflict set from a real merge was exactly one
# path, agents/bravo/journal/2026/07/2026-07-27.md).
# NOT merge=union — this path family FAILS the zero-deleted-lines evidence gate
# stated above: 6185 commits touched it and the probe counts 1980 deleted
# content lines (a floor, since the regex excludes deleted markdown list items),
# so these files are genuinely edited and union would resurrect that history.
# The ayoai-journal-md driver (core/scripts/git-merge-journal-md.sh) instead
# unions by '## heading' SECTION — the markdown analogue of how ayoai-ledger
# unions by record — and still surfaces a REAL conflict when the same heading
# diverges on both sides, so nothing is silently coalesced. Driver registered
# per-clone by install-git-hooks.sh (git driver config is NOT version-controlled).
agents/*/journal/**/*.md merge=ayoai-journal-md

# Cross-box merge routing for the core/config READINGS ledgers. These three .md
# files were extracted OUT of hot-path skills (Aug 2026, hot-path-size-budget
# work) precisely so multiple agents could append dated blocks — i.e. they were
# CREATED as multi-writer append ledgers — and none was given merge routing, so
# `git check-attr merge` returned `unspecified` for all three. Measured
# 2026-08-21 (foxtrot, LAPTOP-3IOFCNEO WSL2): two consecutive integrate attempts
# hit a TRUE content conflict (MERGE_HEAD created — not the dirty-tree defer
# shape) on strategic-scan-readings.md at behind=25, concealing 25 peer commits
# on the ONE box that runs the Roblox worlds. Retry can never clear a content
# conflict (g-115-7048, board msg-20260821-005730-foxtrot-6445).
#
# THE THREE SPLIT ON THE EVIDENCE GATE — deliberately NOT one blanket remedy.
# Probe re-run at decision time per the gate above (git log -p | grep -cE '^-[^-]'):
#   strategic-scan-readings.md   6 commits, 0 deleted content lines -> union OK
#   felt-sense-readings.md       3 commits, 0 deleted content lines -> union OK
#   run-full-suite-baselines.md  7 commits, 2 deleted content lines -> union UNSAFE
# CAVEAT, carried forward deliberately (guard-912): these files are YOUNG (created
# ~2026-08-17..08-19), so a zero over 3-6 commits is a far weaker signal than the
# 6185-commit probe that qualified the journal family above. A young zero is not a
# mature zero — one editorial pass invalidates it. Re-run the probe before widening
# this block, and demote a file to ayoai-journal-md the moment its deleted-line
# count leaves zero. The count is also a FLOOR: the documented regex excludes
# deleted markdown list items.
# SUPERSEDED BY MEASUREMENT 2026-09-16 (g-115-10127), AND ACTED ON 2026-09-18
# (g-115-10132, bravo/cc-05): union is not safe for these ledgers even at zero
# deleted lines. Its zealous refinement emits a line two appended blocks share
# ONCE and interleaves the blocks: merge 10069ea4c0 did that here and dropped a
# ``` fence. The deleted-lines evidence gate above is therefore NOT sufficient
# on its own for a multi-writer append ledger — it measures whether history was
# EDITED, while this defect needs only that two appends SHARE A LINE, which
# formulaic dated blocks do by construction. All three readings ledgers now
# route to merge=ayoai-append-ledger (guard-6868).
core/config/strategic-scan-readings.md merge=ayoai-append-ledger
core/config/felt-sense-readings.md merge=ayoai-append-ledger

# run-full-suite-baselines.md FAILS that union gate (2 deleted content lines) and
# ALSO routed badly the other way: it was on ayoai-journal-md, which unions by
# '## heading' and therefore CONFLICTS on an append that opens no '## ' section —
# measured 28 of 30 replayed pairs. It is a multi-writer baselines TABLE, so it
# joins the other two on merge=ayoai-append-ledger (g-115-10132): exact append
# concatenation, a standard diff3 for any other edit, and a real conflict when
# both sides rewrite the same text. Driver registered per-clone by
# install-git-hooks.sh (git driver config is NOT version-controlled) — an entry
# naming an unregistered driver silently falls back to the default text merge
# (guard-1290), so verify with check-merge-driver-registered.sh on every box.
core/config/run-full-suite-baselines.md merge=ayoai-append-ledger

# merge=ayoai-append-ledger for the readings ledgers that had NO routing
# (g-115-10127). replay-instrument-readings.md wedged cc-05 at behind=37 on
# 2026-09-16: two boxes each appended a dated reading between pushes. Chosen by
# MEASUREMENT, not by the deleted-lines gate above: each file's real history was
# replayed as concurrent appends (base = before commit A, ours = A, theirs = the
# next commit's own change) and merged by each candidate route.
#   file (pairs)                                union               ayoai-journal-md
#   replay-instrument-readings.md (1)           content-equal       clean
#   completion-report-coverage-readings.md (5)  content-equal 5/5   conflict 5/5 (no ## sections)
#   fresh-eyes-shard-readings.md (16)           content-equal 16/16 conflict 15/16
# union looks fine there only because those blocks shared no line; the day two
# blocks share one it interleaves them silently (10069ea4c0, block above).
# ayoai-append-ledger writes ours then theirs verbatim for concurrent appends,
# runs a standard diff3 merge for any other edit, and still conflicts when both
# sides rewrite the same text (core/scripts/git-merge-append-ledger.py).
# Registered per-clone by install-git-hooks.sh; an unregistered clone falls back
# to the default text merge (guard-1290): check-merge-driver-registered.sh.
core/config/replay-instrument-readings.md merge=ayoai-append-ledger
core/config/completion-report-coverage-readings.md merge=ayoai-append-ledger
core/config/fresh-eyes-shard-readings.md merge=ayoai-append-ledger

# Cross-machine merge for the SHARED world/meta stores under .mind-data/ — the
# local-backend (STORAGE_BACKEND=local) analogue of every rule above.
#
# WHY THIS IS NEEDED: with no S3 authority, git IS the sync mechanism — and
# iteration-push.sh's fetch+integrate is NOT backend-gated (zero STORAGE_BACKEND
# refs), so it runs every iteration on every box. Every rule above is scoped to
# agents/*, which WAS the whole git surface while world/ + meta/ were external and
# gitignored. When .mind-data/ became git-tracked (2026-07-28) the shared stores
# entered git with NO merge routing, so git fell back to LINE-based merge — which
# writes '<<<<<<<' markers INSIDE a .jsonl and CORRUPTS it, because a conflict
# marker is not valid JSON. Measured on a real two-box conflict: the unrouted
# store took 2 markers (unparseable); the same conflict routed here merged clean.
#
# WHY ayoai-ledger IS THE RIGHT DRIVER: it dispatches by BASENAME through
# coordination_merge.merge_handler_for() — the SAME 72-handler registry the
# own-cloud S3 reconcile path already uses in production — so each store gets its
# purpose-built commutative handler (merge_aspirations, merge_reasoning_bank,
# merge_guardrails, merge_tree, merge_team_state[_shard], merge_spark_questions,
# merge_append_only_jsonl, ...) with ZERO new merge logic. Verified end-to-end on
# real records: both boxes' new records kept, both counter bumps kept via MAX, and
# a genuine id COLLISION (both boxes allocating rb-900 — the guaranteed clash when
# one agent identity runs on two boxes) auto-resolved to rb-900 + rb-901, no dupes.
#
# AN UNREGISTERED BASENAME NOW DEGRADES SAFELY (g-115-4253, 2026-07-31). merge_bytes
# falls back to git's own 3-way text merge, accepted ONLY when it exits clean AND the
# result still parses (plus a duplicate-YAML-key check). Disjoint edits merge and the
# integrate proceeds; overlapping edits and add/add still exit 1 WITHOUT writing %A, so
# git keeps the conflict and the file retains valid 'ours' content rather than markers.
#
# CORRECTION, kept because the superseded claim is the instructive part. This block
# used to read "AN UNREGISTERED BASENAME IS A STRICT IMPROVEMENT, NOT A RISK ... All
# three cases measured (handled / unhandled / unrouted baseline). So a broad extension
# glob is safe ... no worse than today until then." Every clause was true of the FILE
# and the conclusion was false of the BOX: an unmerged path aborts the whole integrate,
# so ONE unhandled file stops every unrelated commit. cc-06 stranded 54 commits for 6.2h
# behind .mind-data/meta/backpressure.yaml. And "all three cases" was a 2x2 missing its
# fourth cell — ROUTED+disjoint rc=1 (abort) against UNROUTED+disjoint rc=0 (clean, both
# sides kept) is a REGRESSION this glob introduced, invisible to an enumeration that felt
# exhaustive. At fix time 167 of 253 routed files (66%) had no handler, so unregistered
# was the steady state, not a backlog: routing grows by glob, the handler map by hand.
# Registering a handler is still right when a store wants purpose-built commutative
# semantics; it is no longer required merely to stop a wedge. See rb-6054, guard-2108.
#
# NOT merge=union: these are RMW stores (status flips, counter rollups, pruning,
# archival) and fail the zero-deleted-lines evidence gate stated above — union
# would resurrect pruned/edited records.
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT ROUTED: *.md knowledge-tree nodes (prose — a visible conflict
# marker is readable and hand-resolvable, and there is no record structure to
# union), and *.sh / *.py under world/scripts/ (real code — git's line merge is
# the correct behavior there).
#
# KNOWN BOUNDED SIDE-EFFECT: merge_reasoning_bank re-stamps ids via id_format
# 'rb-{N}' (UNPADDED — required by _merge_id_keyed_jsonl's byte-converge contract).
# A store carrying legacy zero-padded rb ids renumbers them on its first real rb
# merge (ZDS: exactly 4 — rb-001..rb-004; the store switches to unpadded at rb-5).
# Record CONTENT is untouched; only textual cross-references go stale. guardrails
# is UNAFFECTED (id_format is 3-pad 'guard-{N:03d}', which already reproduces both
# guard-001 and guard-213 byte-for-byte). Tracked for deliberate normalization —
# not a reason to leave the store unrouted, since the alternative is marker
# corruption of the whole store on every conflict.
.mind-data/world/**/*.jsonl merge=ayoai-ledger
.mind-data/world/**/*.yaml merge=ayoai-ledger
.mind-data/world/**/*.json merge=ayoai-ledger
.mind-data/meta/**/*.jsonl merge=ayoai-ledger
.mind-data/meta/**/*.yaml merge=ayoai-ledger
.mind-data/meta/**/*.json merge=ayoai-ledger
